card.statement:
The $\K$-matrix satisfies the following reflection equation.

\begin{align}
\K_{\bw^2}(a_2) \R(a_1 + a_2) \K_{\bw^1}(a_1) \R(a_1-a_2) & =
\R(a_1-a_2) \K_{\bw^1}(a_1) \R(a_1+a_2) \K_{\bw^2}(a_2),
\end{align}

where the $\K_{\bw^i}(a_i)$'s are understood as $\K_{\bw^1} (a_1) \otimes 1$ and $1\otimes \K_{\bw^2} (a_2)$, respectively.
